{"id":"chatcmpl-17ce898f-ec2c-4b02-b52b-83f7634ded00","object":"chat.completion","created":1795250584,"model":"deepseek-v4.1-flash","choices":[{"index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","reasoning_content":"","content":"```json\n{\n  \"highlights\": \"This task demonstrates a cross-validation strategy for medical image interpretation where ambiguous findings (laterality on a lateral view) are resolved by querying multiple independent expert models with targeted, context-rich questions. The key insight is that lateral views lose left-right discriminability, so the strategy explicitly asks each model to determine laterality rather than assuming it. Agreement between two independent models was used as the confidence signal for the final answer.\",\n  \"patterns\": [\n    \"When image orientation or projection makes a key attribute ambiguous (e.g., laterality on a lateral view), explicitly ask the model to resolve that specific attribute rather than inferring it from the finding alone.\",\n    \"Use two or more independent expert models to answer the same targeted question, and treat their agreement as the confidence signal for the final answer.\",\n    \"Embed relevant metadata (view label, projection type) directly into the query so the model reasons with the correct spatial context.\",\n    \"Decompose the question into a finding-detection step and an attribute-resolution step (e.g., 'is there atelectasis?' then 'which side?') to reduce compound-question errors.\"\n  ],\n  \"playbooks\": {\n    \"Medical imaging QA\": \"Always pass view/projection metadata into the query; when laterality or location is ambiguous on the given view, ask a dedicated attribute-resolution question instead of assuming.\",\n    \"Multi-model consensus\": \"Query at least two independent models with the same well-scoped question; use agreement as the decision rule and disagreement as a signal to escalate or re-query.\",\n    \"Ambiguous-attribute resolution\": \"Identify which attribute (side, segment, level) is hardest to determine from the image, and make that the explicit target of the query rather than a byproduct.\"\n  },\n  \"checklists\": [\n    \"Confirm the image view/projection is included in every model query so spatial reasoning is grounded.\",\n    \"Confirm both models were asked the same laterality-specific question and that their answers agree before finalizing.\"\n  ]\n}\n```"},"finish_reason":"stop","logprobs":null}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":491,"total_tokens":911,"completion_tokens":420,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0,"image_tokens":0,"text_tokens":491},"completion_tokens_details":{"text_tokens":420}}}